{"name":"Fire Dance","hex":"#e3d590","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A (usually self-sustaining) chemical reaction involving the bonding of oxygen with carbon or other fuel, with the production of heat and the presence of flame or smouldering.","An instance of this chemical reaction, especially when intentionally created and maintained in a specific location to a useful end (such as a campfire or a hearth fire)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Amazing; excellent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fire"},{"term":"dance","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sequence of rhythmic steps or movements usually performed to music, for pleasure or as a form of social interaction.","A social gathering where dancing is the main activity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move with rhythmic steps or movements, especially in time to music.","To leap or move lightly and rapidly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fire Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Fire Dance is an album by jazz guitarist Pat Martino, flutist Peter Block, sitar player Ustad Habib Khan, violinist Ilya Rayzman and tabla player Zakir Hussain. It was released in 1997 by Mythos Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/39/Pat_Martino_Fire_Dance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_Dance","wikidata":"Q111939768"},{"title":"Fire Dance (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Fire Dance is an Israeli television drama series created by Rama Burshtein. The Haredi drama stars Mia Irvin, Yehuda Levi and Noa Koler. It is a Yes Studios original series and was broadcast in Israel on Yes Drama. It is streamed internationally by the Jewish streaming service, ChaiFlicks."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_Dance_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q111842203"},{"title":"Fire performance","blocks":[{"text":"Fire performance is a group of performance arts or skills that involve the manipulation of fire. Fire performance typically involves equipment or other objects made with one or more wicks which are designed to sustain a large enough flame to create a visual effect."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Fire_Gypsy_Productions_New_Years_Eve_Fire_Performance.ogv/330px--Fire_Gypsy_Productions_New_Years_Eve_Fire_Performance.ogv.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_performance","wikidata":"Q1186323"},{"title":"Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Fire is the rapid oxidation of a fuel in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.\nFlames, the most visible portion of the fire, are produced in the combustion reaction when the fuel reaches its ignition point temperature. Flames from hydrocarbon fuels consist primarily of carbon dioxide, water vapor, oxygen, and nitrogen. If hot enough, the gases may become ionized to produce plasma. The color and intensity of the flame depend on the type of fuel and composition of the surrounding gases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Large_bonfire.jpg/330px-Large_bonfire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire","wikidata":"Q3196"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Yehuda_Levi_2.jpg/500px-Yehuda_Levi_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Yehuda_Levi_2.jpg/1280px-Yehuda_Levi_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Yehuda_Levi_2.jpg/500px-Yehuda_Levi_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Yehuda Levi stars as Natan.","link":"https://e